<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="093" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Reorder the 7 Create wizards: collect IsSecure → create record → provision-if-secure → upload → link</title>
    <phase>0c Secure Documents — upload path decomposition</phase>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Changes the order of operations in every Create wizard and is the change that closes a real tenant-isolation gap. Getting the order wrong writes customer documents into a shared container.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>The judgement is sequencing across 7 wizards with a provisioning step that cannot move, plus deciding which of two existing Secure UI components is live per wizard. A wrong pick produces a fix that never renders.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <effort-reason>Brownfield across 7 wizards with a shared service; the reorder interacts with pre-fill, provisioning and the record-keyed upload contract simultaneously.</effort-reason>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Touches EntityCreationService plus all 7 wizards; concurrent edits to the shared creation service produce a silent merge mess.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>076</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, frontend, auth, pcf</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-3 days</estimated-effort>
    <origin>notes/plan-upload-path-decomposition-2026-08-31.md §3. Owner-directed 2026-08-31: "for the Secure Project UI it is a part of this solution so need to include it."</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Today a secure Matter created WITH documents puts those documents in the shared BU container, because at upload time no matter exists yet to be secure. Server-side container derivation alone cannot fix that — only reordering the wizard can.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE full-stack engineer.</role>

  <goal>In every Create wizard, the owning record exists and has been provisioned (if secure) BEFORE any bytes move, so the server derives the container from a record it authorized.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>`EntityCreationService.ts` orders the flow **upload → create → link**. At upload time
there is no record, so the container defaults to the acting user's BU (`applyUserBuDefaults`). For a
SECURE record that is the isolation gap: the documents land in the shared container and stay there.

**The reorder is what closes it.** Target order: collect IsSecure early → create the record →
provision the container if secure → upload against `(entity, recordId)` → create the document rows.

⚠️ **Provisioning REQUIRES the record to already exist** (task 008 finding: its final act is an
`UpdateAsync` stamping three fields on the project). So IsSecure is *collected* early and *acted on*
after creation. These are compatible; the order cannot be inverted.

⚠️ This is also why abandoning the wizard leaves **no orphaned container** — nothing is provisioned
until the record exists.

⚠️ `provision-project` is **project-only**. Owner: projects first, **matters as a later add-on**.

🔴 **DO NOT AUTHOR A NEW SECURE PROJECT UI.** A 2026-08-31 note claimed the Secure Project wizard step
"was never specified". That is WRONG — it exists in **two** implementations, and there is already a
pending task **068** to rework it:
  - `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateProjectWizard/SecureProjectSection.tsx`
  - `src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/components/CreateProject/SecureProjectSection.tsx`
  - `tasks/068-create-project-wizard-secure-step.poml` (pending, Phase 4, FR-31)

Per CLAUDE.md §11 (extend, do not fork), this task owns something NARROWER: move the IsSecure
COLLECTION POINT earlier (owner: before the Info step) so the flag is known before record creation,
and REUSE the existing section component where it renders. Whether that means depending on 068,
folding 068 in, or landing first and letting 068 rework what moved is this task's sequencing call —
but duplicating the component is not on the menu.

⚠️ **Two copies is itself an open question to SURFACE, not silently resolve.** Determine which is live
for each of the 7 wizards before editing either; changing the wrong one produces a fix that never
renders.

**Why the reorder is safe w.r.t. AI pre-fill** (the finding that makes it possible): pre-fill uploads
to a server-configured STAGING container (`SpeOptions.StagingContainerId`, verified
`MatterPreFillService.cs:307`), and the final document upload is a SEPARATE browser call holding the
same `File` objects. The two legs are independent, so moving the final upload after record creation
does not disturb field extraction. Bytes travel twice — true today as well, so not a regression.</background>

    <ship-together>🔴 Client and BFF MUST deploy together — no compatibility window. BFF-first 404s every
upload; client-first 404s every upload. This MUST appear in the PR description.</ship-together>
  </context>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/plan-upload-path-decomposition-2026-08-31.md</file>
      <file>projects/unified-access-control-r2/tasks/076-record-keyed-upload-contract.poml</file>
      <file>projects/unified-access-control-r2/tasks/068-create-project-wizard-secure-step.poml</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/EntityCreationService.ts</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Re-derive at current HEAD: the 7 wizards, which Secure section component each actually renders, and whether 076 has landed the record-keyed route. Do NOT inherit any of these from the plan note — it has been wrong twice already.</step>
    <step order="1">Decide and RECORD the 068 sequencing (depend / fold in / land first). State it in the PR.</step>
    <step order="2">Move the IsSecure collection point ahead of the Info step, reusing the existing section component.</step>
    <step order="3">Reorder `EntityCreationService`: create → provision-if-secure → upload against `(entity, recordId)` → link.</step>
    <step order="4">Verify pre-fill still extracts fields (staging leg untouched).</step>
    <step order="5">Prove the isolation fix: a secure record created WITH documents puts them in the record's own container, not the shared BU one. This is the acceptance test that matters.</step>
    <step order="6">Verify abandoning the wizard provisions nothing.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the two Secure section components turn out to be BOTH live across different wizards, STOP and surface it — consolidating them is its own change and may belong to 068.</trigger>
    <trigger>If provisioning turns out to be reachable before record creation in any path, STOP — the whole premise of the ordering is that it is not.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>`EntityCreationService` already owns create/upload/link; `SecureProjectSection.tsx` already renders the secure choice; `provision-project` already provisions.</existing>
    <extension>Pure reordering plus moving a collection point. No new service, no new component — the explicit anti-goal here is authoring a second Secure UI.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A secure Matter created with documents puts those documents in the shared BU container permanently. That is the exact isolation failure this project exists to close, and server-side container derivation cannot reach it.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">7 Create wizards reordered; IsSecure collected before the Info step</output>
    <output type="test">Isolation test: secure record + documents → record's own container</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>All 7 Create wizards create the record before any upload.</criterion>
    <criterion>A secure record created WITH documents places them in that record's own container — asserted by test, not inspection.</criterion>
    <criterion>No NEW Secure Project UI component exists; the existing one is reused and the 068 relationship is recorded.</criterion>
    <criterion>Abandoning any wizard provisions no container and leaves no orphan.</criterion>
    <criterion>AI pre-fill still extracts fields (staging leg unaffected).</criterion>
    <criterion>PR description carries the ship-together statement and the Placement Justification.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>NOT STARTED. Depends on 076 landing the record-keyed contract this uploads against.</notes>
</task>
